                        "sense_id": "fbeb7d32-8da0-3fb3-9b53-5a885c2899ec",
                        "entry_id": "6ee2d7f6-0cd1-3cc5-a44c-44615d8ee0ab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Located behind (further towards the rear than) the middle."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e878e59e-f980-48db-a491-c6f1b0d5dc87",
                                "sense_id": "fbeb7d32-8da0-3fb3-9b53-5a885c2899ec",
                                "text": "Head, thorax, and abdomen yellow and white. Fore wing white, with the costal half to end of cell suffused with fuscous; an obscure fuscous triangular postmedial mark with its apex on inner margin, its inner limb with a black speck […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "97182bb9-8a17-308f-ad1f-353d2f9d0619",
                        "entry_id": "6ee2d7f6-0cd1-3cc5-a44c-44615d8ee0ab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Located after the medial element."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d56d03a7-34a8-49c1-b693-20840879b39d",
                                "sense_id": "97182bb9-8a17-308f-ad1f-353d2f9d0619",
                                "text": "[…] and PA *naːwal(a)w- and Y noːʔrep- 'following one behind the other' 055 (where PA adds postmedial *-(a)w, and Yurok the intransitive final -ep)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "48932eb4-209e-4d97-ad4b-f3b5b6c62cd7",
                                "sense_id": "97182bb9-8a17-308f-ad1f-353d2f9d0619",
                                "text": "The medial suffix, ...kon..., carries the meaning \"day\": e.g., n'ka-nîšokonin I'll be away two days (and nights). […] The suffix also occurs with a postmedial extension, ...ak: e.g., nîšokonakisiw niski-pîsim it is the second day of April […] literally, the goose moon is in a state (...si-) of day two."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
